  "guideHowSentenceTitle": "Read today's sentence",
  "guideHowSentenceStep1": "Open the Learn tab to see today's sentence. Sentences come in sets of up to five, with your progress shown at the top.",
  "guideHowSentenceStep3": "Gold words are the ones you're learning. The quiz asks about them.",
  "guideHowSentenceStep4": "Tap the sentence card to open the detail screen.",
  "guideHowDetailTitle": "The detail screen",
  "guideHowDetailLead": "The detail screen explains the context, style, spelling, and tones. Linking these clues makes words easier to remember.",
  "guideHowSoundTitle": "Listen and say it aloud",
  "guideHowSoundStep1": "“Listen to the model” plays the sentence on a loop.",
  "guideHowSoundStep2": "In “Pronunciation practice,” press and hold “Hold to speak” while reading the sentence aloud. Your tones are checked immediately.",
  "guideHowSoundStep3": "Green means correct, amber means close, and red means incorrect. Tap a word to compare your pitch with the model and see how to improve.",
  "guideHowQuizTitle": "Take the check quiz",
  "guideHowQuizStep1": "Tap “Check what you learned” below the sentence to start the check quiz.",
  "guideHowQuizStep2": "Choose the meaning of the gold word from four options.",
  "guideHowQuizStep3": "After answering, review the word's meaning and usage.",
  "guideHowQuizStep4": "Then move to the next sentence. After the last one in the set, the summary quiz begins.",
  "guideHowReviewQuizTitle": "Take the summary quiz",
  "guideHowReviewQuizStep1": "After each set of up to five sentences, choose the missing word in a sentence you've studied.",
  "guideHowReviewQuizStep2": "Sentences return for review after one day, three days, one week, and longer intervals. Words you haven't mastered appear first.",
  "guideHowReviewQuizStep3": "Tap the hint once for pronunciation and again for the translation. Correct answers without hints raise your score faster.",
  "guideHowReviewQuizStep4": "Not sure? “Check the sentence” takes you back to it.",
  "guideHowReviewQuizStep5": "Correct answers count toward your vocabulary score.",
